Computing cross product for normal vector...
Simplifying normal components...
n_raw (unnormalized):
  n[0] = -sin(s)*sin(t)/2
  n[1] = sin(t)*cos(s)/2
  n[2] = sin(s/2)*cos(t)
  n[3] = -cos(s/2)*cos(t)

|n|^2 = 1 - 3*sin(t)**2/4
|n|^2 simplified = 1 - 3*sin(t)**2/4

f = 1 - 3*sin(t)**2/4

Killing field normal components (times |n_raw|/R):
  <X13, n_raw>/R = sin(s/2)*cos(s)*cos(t)**2 + sin(s)*sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)/2
  <X14, n_raw>/R = sin(s/2)*sin(s)*sin(t)**2/2 - cos(s/2)*cos(s)*cos(t)**2
  <X23, n_raw>/R = sin(s/2)*sin(s)*cos(t)**2 - sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)*cos(s)/2
  <X24, n_raw>/R = -sin(s/2)*sin(t)**2*cos(s)/2 - sin(s)*cos(s/2)*cos(t)**2


Now decomposing into Fourier modes in s...

=== Direct computation ===

X13: p[0]*n[2] - p[2]*n[0] = sin(s/2)*cos(s)*cos(t)**2 + sin(s)*sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)/2
  coeff of cos(1s/2): sin(s)*sin(t)**2/2
  coeff of sin(1s/2): cos(s)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of cos(1s): sin(s/2)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of sin(1s): sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)/2

X14: p[0]*n[3] - p[3]*n[0] = sin(s/2)*sin(s)*sin(t)**2/2 - cos(s/2)*cos(s)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of cos(1s/2): -cos(s)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of sin(1s/2): sin(s)*sin(t)**2/2
  coeff of cos(1s): -cos(s/2)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of sin(1s): sin(s/2)*sin(t)**2/2

X23: p[1]*n[2] - p[2]*n[1] = sin(s/2)*sin(s)*cos(t)**2 - sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)*cos(s)/2
  coeff of cos(1s/2): -sin(t)**2*cos(s)/2
  coeff of sin(1s/2): sin(s)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of cos(1s): -sin(t)**2*cos(s/2)/2
  coeff of sin(1s): sin(s/2)*cos(t)**2

X24: p[1]*n[3] - p[3]*n[1] = -sin(s/2)*sin(t)**2*cos(s)/2 - sin(s)*cos(s/2)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of cos(1s/2): -sin(s)*cos(t)**2
  coeff of sin(1s/2): -sin(t)**2*cos(s)/2
  coeff of cos(1s): -sin(s/2)*sin(t)**2/2
  coeff of sin(1s): -cos(s/2)*cos(t)**2
